Task: capabilities + docs (plan agui_hitl_interrupts_a1f3c2d8, phase P5)

Why: spec FR6 and FR7.

Changes:
- agui/capabilities.go: HumanInTheLoopCapabilities.InterruptReasons
  ([]string, json interruptReasons); SupportedInterruptReasons() helper;
  MergeInterruptCapabilities fills it only when nil.
- agui/capabilities_reasons_test.go (new): defaults, merge fills,
  merge preserves a host's list, and the JSON key.
- agui/doc.go: new 'Non-tool interrupts' and 'Multiple interrupts per
  event' sections; Limitations rewritten; capabilities line updated.

Design note: the merge deliberately does not append the defaults to a
host-supplied list. A host with a custom classifier emits reasons the
launcher cannot enumerate, and appending tool_call/input_required/
confirmation would advertise reasons that host may never produce.

Documentation decisions worth keeping:
- Recorded the workflow-agent constraint from the spec Background. Only
  the workflow scheduler populates resumeInputs and only
  agent/workflowagent.detectResume routes the reply, so a plain llmagent
  cannot produce adk_request_input. Without this, a host would reasonably
  expect prompting an llmagent to work.
- Recorded that clients must answer EVERY interrupt in
  outcome.interrupts. Before this track only one was ever sent, so
  existing clients may assume a single-element array; validation rejects
  a resume that leaves any pending interrupt unaddressed.
- Stated that the launcher never emits adk_request_input itself (spec
  non-goal), so hosts know the emission is theirs to write.

The TODO(non-tool-interrupts) comment is gone from the tree; it was
removed in fff6fb3 when the handler was registered.

